# A17.var06 independent prospective contract review

Decision: **GO_CONSTRUCTION_ONLY** for the frozen A17.var06 prospective contract. This authorizes case and proof-method construction. It does not approve a native launch, preflight outcome, publication, or Issue 18 completion.

The governing contract is `tmp/a17-var06-prospective-v100-20261009-01/contract.json` (7,613 bytes, SHA256 `58c12480998f691b619f305922eace2eb1b4aede71fbb779de77ad0085bb15e7`) with oracle map (4,168 bytes, SHA256 `e1e713ec003cf0d2cba62e38161cd57c504161b3503b624f63d0e33067a40371`) and README (3,151 bytes, SHA256 `529095708ff340d17d9878ed37fb28a84c33e509b9d9a2528673faa61dcab1fc`). The independent RO audit method `tmp/a17-var06-independent-prospective-audit-v101-20261009.py` is 8,993 bytes/SHA256 `e11aed8ca116d0bc6afdd177be0317ac43779e98a91c263974ff4c4606628952`. Its one original capture at `tmp/i04-var09-root-review-proofs-v100-20261008/a17-var06-independent-prospective-v101-20261008T184036806321Z-eb0b8cf5/receipt.json` is 1,370 bytes/SHA256 `f8d76246b13dc684b926927889521c24da51f4e7e3520cac1dd082db5c1ac3f1`: actual exit 0, source and capture methods stable, stdout 111 bytes/SHA256 `baf2a04fcd797027ec68b3fd77f03748aac603c9ac68263d51a205267147f13c`, stderr 0/SHA256 `e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855`. The original stdout says `PASS_A17_VAR06_PROSPECTIVE_ONLY pairs59 originals66 log60/52 report4966 soleSTOTD control0 predicted1 native0`.

The accepted A17 native input has two `UnitGroupMember` rows, each with XTIME 0, one aircraft in each unit, and a two-system group mission. Its sealed 60-line/52-timed physical log allocates both numeric aircraft to that mission. The proposed authored and exported deltas change only the second unit's XTIME from 0 to 1, with all metadata and other cells held exactly to their pinned accepted parent representations. Manual physical pages 313–314 say XTIME is determined from the systems actually used and reported when the mission launches; page 567 defines STOTD as their summed delay. The accepted J07 `group.sxs` instrumentation used the accepted A17 `model.sxo`: J07 invocation and closure both pin SXO SHA256 `f4c2fcd42c5620ec6e7adf163962bb6001a4a9acf49eee8d7adfeba50113349b` and settings SHA256 `e78466cc27d8c213e4d9bf4ed0065844471593069e81abe665cbd7fa4e9172ea`. Its sealed A17 group control has eight ordered tables and 4,966 typed cells; the sole `FixedMissionResults.STOTD` cell is declared double and has control value 0. The prospective expected value is 1.

The full physical log byte equality and equality of the other 4,965 report cells are strict predeclared, falsifiable hypotheses. The manual does not establish those broad equalities. Any changed log line, other report cell, topology, source/export cell, metadata, converter diagnostic, or failed provenance gate is **NO_GO** for this contract. No postrun fitting or alternate branch acceptance is authorized. The J07 report-only run supplies observation settings and a pinned control from the same accepted A17 SXO; it is not a behavioral parent. The result cannot be generalized to another selection branch, continuous missions, physical travel, GUI behavior, or the whole issue.

The root selection receipt `tmp/a17-var06-root-selection-v100-20261008/20261008T182533111132Z-300daf73/receipt.json` (SHA256 `04d57600dd94386e2fd929bc3b01e2eab5f5c5cb21f23f130399b46a0dbfa7c2`) independently sealed and checked 59 disk/Git source pairs and 66 mandatory originals with bytes/attributes. This auditor verifies their recorded counts and its selected source/control pins; it does not itself rehash every 59 pair or 66 original. Fresh source, manual/dictionary/executable, GUI/session/mutex, unique path, pure check, actual SSH preflight, strict 17-line converter, exact original stream and receipt binding, and an independent postrun replay remain required before any bounded runtime acceptance.

The earlier 8,969-byte v100 auditor was preserved RO and never executed. Its relative-to-absolute package comparison was corrected in v101 before the sole original capture; the contract/oracle bytes were unchanged.